      "side": 1,
      "message": "The way Alex says this makes sense. I think what confuses me is the header documentation for isPreferredConfiguration:\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\nChecks if this configuration should be discarded in favor of another configuration created from the same context.\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\n\nSo Alex is saying that isPreferred simply changes order (which makes sense), but the docs say that isPreferred discards the target configuration (which implies replacement)\n\nAre the docs bad? Or am I misreading something?",
